    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d140">

                <pb facs="0192" n="180" sameAs="frus:frus1941v02/pg180"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.51/158</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum of Conversation, by the Secretary of
                        State</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-05-21">May 21, 1941</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The British Ambassador called at his request. I related to him the substance of
                    my talk with the French Ambassador on yesterday, all of which he heartily
                    approved.</p>
                <p>He then inquired as to whether we felt as though we could recognize De Gaulle in
                    any more conspicuous way than heretofore. I replied that, of course, we were
                    seeking to salvage whatever we could from the situation of Weygand in Africa,
                    and from the Government at Vichy, and that if Weygand should stand up, De Gaulle
                    would have to become subordinate. To this he agreed.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>C[<hi rendition="#small-caps">ordell</hi>] H[<hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >ull</hi>]</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
